From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:55:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: add Gemini LK CPU clock rates

Planet's retained MT6797 LK walks every enabled CPU node before Image
decompression.  Its iterator advances only after reading clock-frequency,
so a missing property on the first CPU makes the loader select that same
node forever.

Add the exact rates from the runtime-proven Gemini Stage-27 device tree.
These properties describe the loader input and do not enable a CPU, add a
clock consumer, or change Linux CPU admission.  The board continues to
boot with maxcpus=8 while the two Cortex-A72 CPUs remain closed.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -142,6 +142,46 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&cpu0 {
+	clock-frequency = <1391000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	clock-frequency = <1391000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	clock-frequency = <1391000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	clock-frequency = <1391000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu4 {
+	clock-frequency = <1950000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu5 {
+	clock-frequency = <1950000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu6 {
+	clock-frequency = <1950000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu7 {
+	clock-frequency = <1950000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu8 {
+	clock-frequency = <2288000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu9 {
+	clock-frequency = <2288000000>;
+};
+
 &mt6351regulator {
 	mt6351_vemc_reg: ldo-vemc {
 		regulator-name = "vemc_3v3";
